<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">That icy wind rattling the rafters is the =
cold reality of what follows the closure of the transfer window, a hungover=
 pall of regret. Despite <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.co=
m/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDom6Up7NBgS48fUZgZf5c=
eBLKr42K4LHJzFlvuGW4qxFxx5Qu3ze4S9zrQoC9tL-7_aJmPmRiofOXFCKTpXjkfj7njeriE1C=
lAA2qla7PaptNIv8vwM866vbDSx8SubJziAwes4B_Yso-TORw-K2DPJhcziNFiRwquo810f9axe=
JAhAOboCReeQOQoyJmvQfxz-LP4cixyi1juQr40-OxmNAHrWcfGl5Z9ieDG2h5CNPIRyDhfBz-m=
kHMx8VHc9KNfaKypYYVydkvabFC7NgNtCdZSPtM80W8Lc_xxOlSDUA/4tr/Ac2BGRD7RMK6xIEf=
25QV3g/h29/h001.bfY_CoxkmmMLK4rNskuL-YNI5EFI9uXRPOqEoZvDdx4" style=3D"color=
: #0077B6;">=C2=A33.5bn shelled out</a> in the men=E2=80=99s window, severa=
l things will <em>not</em> be happening in the Premier League when they mig=
ht have been. When Arsenal host Chelsea for a most super of Sundays, Vin=C3=
=ADcius J=C3=BAnior will <em>not</em> be playing in their attack, and neith=
er will Gabriel Martinelli, whose lengthy social media disgrace farewells o=
n <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFu=
ifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg28XRJ-yuNXtortbywHON3z=
bhhxUBKtIdCF0Nqx3mIuUSx5VSPTLgkbxzhC1QnyJpSBlYCl2du4K-tP55npSUH-iIFJ_sisD5U=
LfIRHDTZVmZXtaYzWeWPlvMaB5641HXEZhPWl_ZJ6eLUOfDhLDZQgqAoQ6izdOxMPryT4p12aB5=
kSq2KLfo_ga1whJGlWaURwpTp8F10VIRop5s8st2uH9oBE7IncatBjzTbACepdE/4tr/Ac2BGRD=
7RMK6xIEf25QV3g/h30/h001.lHdCx0_3wqX-TjJPy2UO8QAJrf3Fh4y3-EHvC71kdvU" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">his departure for Saudi Arabia</a> pointedly made no m=
ention of Mikel Arteta.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There will be no Enzo Fern=C3=A1ndez for C=
helsea, with him joining what he called a =E2=80=9Cbig club=E2=80=9D in Man=
chester City and in his stead, Lamine Camara will <em>not</em> be lining up=
 in Chelsea=E2=80=99s midfield. On Monday, the majority of Chelsea fans kne=
w very little about Camara but now they yearn desperately, a love unrequite=
d for the 22-year-old Senegalese tyro who, it says here, once played for Me=
tz. Should the Gunners grind through the gears on Sunday, as is entirely po=
ssible, expect to hear criticism of sporting director Andrea Berta. A most =
modern phenomenon is suits having their names taken in vain. Liverpool trav=
el to Ipswich later on Friday with fans wailing at a lack of cover at full-=
back. Richard Hughes, also off to Saudi, may well have ears burning when a =
year ago the Reds=E2=80=99 supporters were asking for his autograph. He wil=
l receive little thanks for Liverpool having the highest net spend in the l=
eague when the midfield is slow as a coach.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The same could be said of Jason Wilcox if =
Manchester United fans were able to scan his name into a song. Their red-sh=
irted heroes will <em>not</em> feature Newcastle=E2=80=99s Lewis Hall when =
they face Everton on Sunday. Though having no obvious replacement should Lu=
ke Shaw suffer hamstring-twang is nothing on the personnel deficit at Hill =
Dickinson Stadium. Fans=E2=80=99 wishes for Harrison Armstrong to stay were=
 met but he no longer has Iliman Ndiaye to pass to, while Thierno Barry is =
the sole striker available to David Moyes. That Everton currently own more =
stadiums than strikers has become a hoary old gag within days of the club=
=E2=80=99s deadline-day disasters. Folarin Balogun, the erstwhile Evertonia=
n, will <em>not</em> be playing for Monaco against PSG this weekend, and ne=
ither will he play for the club in Tin Pot.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Richarlison, having hoped to return to Eve=
rton, will also <em>not</em> be playing this weekend for Tottenham at Notti=
ngham Forest, having been tinned entirely from Spurs=E2=80=99 Premier Leagu=
e squad. His SMD post that =E2=80=9Cdespite this turmoil, I am under contra=
ct at Spurs and will remain at the club=E2=80=99s disposal=E2=80=9D was fol=
lowed by them trying to dispose of him. Mohamed Salah=E2=80=99s Trabzonspor=
 is a reported destination as well as the usual Saudi escape hatch. Balogun=
 looks to be heading for the Turkish Super Lig or the Saudi Pro League, too=
. The funny thing about regret is that it=E2=80=99s better to regret someth=
ing you have done than to regret something you haven=E2=80=99t done.</p>
